      "component_id": "ED26-BM-RAT2021-4-3-C03",
      "verdict": "partial",
      "gap": "Present Merin's Linda example with its empirical boundary. Merin 2021 p.273 reports the finding that a surprisingly large proportion of respondents ranked feminist bank teller above bank teller (a late-1970s task, no counts given), and the design-and-explication step that the description E was designed to be representative of F and unrepresentative of B, with representativeness explicated as the relevance of 'Linda is F' to E. That step is what links the experiment to the covert-relevance reading. rationality-4-3.tex lines 474-504 give the ranking task and an editorial model. w02b-p15-024.tex lines 871-887 give the note-19 pointers. Neither states the reported result or the representativeness step, and 024 lines 879-881 say that Merin reports no task for either phenomenon, although p.273 describes the Linda ranking task.",
